-- ============================================================================
-- Bug ako/mxcli#259: a mapping's schema source was never resolved
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Symptom (before fix):
--   `create import mapping X with json structure Module.NoSuchThing` was
--   accepted and written verbatim. mxbuild reports the dangling reference as
--   CE1613 "… no longer exists" — but only at build time; `mxcli check` and even
--   `check --references` passed.
--
-- Worse than it looks — the typo turned OFF member validation:
--   The schema index is empty whenever the structure cannot be loaded FOR ANY
--   REASON, and `resolvable()` reads an empty index as "there is nothing to
--   validate against". So ONE typo in the source name switched off every member
--   check in the mapping, and this went through with no complaint at all:
--
--     create import mapping M.IM with json structure M.NoSuchThing
--     { create M.Loc { LocId = nonsense } };     -- both wrong, both accepted
--
--   That is why the fix refuses at the SOURCE rather than making `resolvable()`
--   stricter: a NAMED but unresolvable source is an error, while NO source at
--   all — an XML schema, a message definition, a schema-less test mapping —
--   must keep working.
--
-- Also fixed: `null values` is an enum, not free text.
--   ExportMappings$NullValueOption is {LeaveOutElement, SendAsNil}; mxcli wrote
--   whatever identifier it was given, so `null values Banana` reached the stored
--   document verbatim.
--
-- The XML half, since fixed:
--   `with xml schema Module.NoSuchThing` was written through the same way. It
--   now resolves against ListXmlSchemas on both engines. The silent-disabling
--   half never applied there — mxcli cannot read an XSD's element tree, so an
--   XML mapping had no member validation to lose — leaving the plain dangling
--   reference, CE1613.
--
--   There is no fixture for it HERE and cannot be: MDL cannot create an XML
--   schema, so a bug test has nothing to reference. The rule is pinned by unit
--   tests instead (mdl/executor/mapping_source_resolution_test.go and
--   sdk/mpr/reader_xmlschema_test.go).
--
--   How the document shape was established, since no reference existed: NONE of
--   the nine demo apps in the corpus contains an XML schema. A synthetic
--   XmlSchemas$XmlSchema unit was planted instead, and mxbuild 11.13.0 asked
--   whether it was the thing it resolves against — the mapping's reference went
--   from CE1613 "The selected XML schema 'XGap.Probe_Xsd' no longer exists" to
--   CE0292 "Please import an XSD file." at XML schema 'XGap.Probe_Xsd', which is
--   mxbuild naming, by module and name, the document it had just found.
--
--   That measurement is also why the XML check FAILS OPEN on an empty list: a
--   project with no XML schemas is the ordinary case, not evidence of a typo.
--
-- Watch for:
--   An EMPTY project and a backend that CANNOT LIST look identical from here.
--   Refusing is right for the first and wrong for the second, so the refusal
--   only fires when the listing succeeds; a listing error takes the name at face
--   value. Two pre-existing mock tests named a structure their mock did not
--   provide and started failing — the right fix was to give the mock the
--   structure, not to weaken the check, since a mapping whose named source does
--   not exist is an inconsistent model to be asserting against.
--
-- Validation:
--   mxbuild 11.13 reports 0 errors on the good mappings below; the bad forms are
--   refused by `exec` AND by `check -p`, each naming what would have worked.
--   `check -p` catching them is new: the issue's own report was that both check
--   tiers passed, and the JSON half shipped refusing only at exec.
-- ============================================================================

create module BugTest259;

create persistent entity BugTest259.Loc ( LocId: String(100) );

create json structure BugTest259.JSON_Loc
  snippet $${"locationId": "x"}$$;

-- The control: a source that resolves, and a member that exists.
create or modify import mapping BugTest259.IMM_Loc
  folder 'Mappings'
  with json structure BugTest259.JSON_Loc
{
  create BugTest259.Loc { LocId = locationId }
};

-- The enum, spelled correctly. `null values Banana` is now refused.
create or modify export mapping BugTest259.EXM_Loc
  folder 'Mappings'
  with json structure BugTest259.JSON_Loc
  null values SendAsNil
{
  BugTest259.Loc { locationId = LocId }
};
